/* chc.independence.gcm_test's in-sample shrink: what the clusters' sums of residual products
   spread when the residuals are fitted in the rows they are tested on.

   e, f independent with i.i.d. rows of variance 1, H the hat matrix of the regression's design of
   rank r over n rows, M = I - H, the residuals M e and M f, the products p_i = (M e)_i (M f)_i.

   STEP 1  E[(M e)(M e)'] = M M' = M: M is symmetric and idempotent.
   STEP 2  A cluster's sum S_c = sum_{i in c} p_i has E S_c^2 = sum_{i,j in c} M_ij^2 = |M_cc|_F^2,
           and sum_c |M_cc|_F^2 = n - 2 r + sum_c |H_cc|_F^2 (the diagonal of H sums to r).
   STEP 3  The total sum_i p_i has variance |M|_F^2 = n - r.
   STEP 4  The shrink, sqrt of STEP 2 over STEP 3, at a design of 1, x, x^2 over x = 0..6 and
           clusters {1,2}, {3,4,5}, {6,7}, exactly; the float is what _in_sample_shrink returns on
           the same design and labels.

   Run: timeout 120 maxima --very-quiet -Q -b validation/gcm_in_sample_shrink.mac */

display2d : false$

xs : makelist(k, k, 0, 6)$
n : length(xs)$
X : apply(matrix, makelist([1, x, x^2], x, xs))$
H : X . invert(transpose(X) . X) . transpose(X)$
M : ident(n) - H$
r : 3$
clusters : [[1, 2], [3, 4, 5], [6, 7]]$
frob2(A, rows) := lsum(lsum(A[i, j]^2, j, rows), i, rows)$

print("STEP 1 M M' - M (expect zero matrix):", ratsimp(M . transpose(M) - M))$
print("STEP 1 trace of H less r (expect 0):", ratsimp(lsum(H[i, i], i, makelist(i, i, 1, n)) - r))$
within_m : lsum(frob2(M, c), c, clusters)$
within_h : lsum(frob2(H, c), c, clusters)$
print("STEP 2 sum_c |M_cc|^2 less n - 2 r + sum_c |H_cc|^2 (expect 0):",
      ratsimp(within_m - (n - 2 * r + within_h)))$
print("STEP 3 |M|_F^2 less n - r (expect 0):", ratsimp(frob2(M, makelist(i, i, 1, n)) - (n - r)))$
shrink : sqrt(ratsimp((n - 2 * r + within_h) / (n - r)))$
print("STEP 4 shrink, exact:", shrink, " float:", float(shrink))$
